From 1645bff536216317bc2130fbb75b6c0806db2cf7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alan Steremberg <alan.steremberg@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 11:39:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] rusty-backup: Cedar name-directory entries need
 File.FP.da, not just the FileID

Cedar's directory enumeration died on the first entry with
  FS.Error $badFP -- 'File.FP from directory/cache doesn't correspond to
  a local volume'
and every later entry was lost with it, so a 1200-file volume listed
three files and stopped.

Cause, from Cedar's own sources rather than guesswork:
  File.mesa      FP: MACHINE DEPENDENT RECORD[id(0): FileID, da(2): DA]
  FileImpl.mesa  Open builds VolumeFormat.LogicalRun[first: fp.da,
                 size: headerPages] and hands it to TranslateLogicalRun
  FSMainImpl2    raises $badFP when OpenFile rejects the FP
So fp.da is the LOGICAL PAGE of the file's header within the volume. The
writer left it 0 -- which points every entry at logical page 0, the
volume root -- with the comment 'fp.da left 0'.

build_client_directory now writes it and parse_client_directory reads it
back; set_client_directory resolves each entry's header page (the same
identification add_file stamps into the label) before the B-tree becomes
a file, and drops an entry it cannot resolve rather than emitting a null
da, since one bad entry costs every entry after it. No public API change.

Tests: the build/parse round trip now asserts fp.da survives, and the
full-stack test asserts each named file resolves to its own non-zero
header page. 15 Pilot tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
